## 🚀 Load Balancing

### Load Balancer Configuration
```javascript
// Load balancer for multiple instances
const loadBalancer = {
  instances: [
    { id: 1, host: 'localhost', port: 3001, weight: 1, active: true },
    { id: 2, host: 'localhost', port: 3002, weight: 1, active: true },
    { id: 3, host: 'localhost', port: 3003, weight: 1, active: true }
  ],
  
  // Round-robin with health checking
  getNextInstance: () => {
    const activeInstances = this.instances.filter(instance => instance.active);
    if (activeInstances.length === 0) {
      throw new Error('No active instances available');
    }
    
    // Simple round-robin
    const index = Math.floor(Math.random() * activeInstances.length);
    return activeInstances[index];
  },
  
  // Health check for instances
  healthCheck: async (instance) => {
    try {
      const response = await fetch(`http://${instance.host}:${instance.port}/api/health`);
      const data = await response.json();
      
      instance.active = data.status === 'healthy';
      instance.lastCheck = new Date();
      
      return instance.active;
      } catch (error) {
      instance.active = false;
      instance.lastCheck = new Date();
      return false;
    }
  },
  
  // Periodic health checking
  startHealthChecks: () => {
    setInterval(async () => {
      for (const instance of this.instances) {
        await this.healthCheck(instance);
      }
    }, 30000); // Check every 30 seconds
  }
};
```

## 📊 Performance Best Practices

### 1. Database Best Practices
- Use prepared statements to prevent SQL injection
- Implement proper indexing for frequently queried columns
- Use connection pooling to manage database connections
- Monitor slow queries and optimize them
- Use pagination for large result sets

### 2. Caching Best Practices
- Cache frequently accessed data
- Implement cache invalidation strategies
- Use appropriate TTL values
- Monitor cache hit rates
- Use Redis for distributed caching

### 3. API Best Practices
- Implement rate limiting
- Use compression for large responses
- Implement proper error handling
- Use async/await for better performance
- Monitor API response times

### 4. Frontend Best Practices
- Use React Query for data fetching and caching
- Implement lazy loading for components
- Use code splitting for better bundle sizes
- Implement proper error boundaries
- Use memoization for expensive calculations

### 5. Monitoring Best Practices
- Implement comprehensive logging
- Use performance monitoring tools
- Set up alerts for performance issues
- Regular performance audits
- Monitor resource usage